  "term": "neuropathy",
  "definition": "Neuropathy is a disorder of the cranial nerves or the peripheral nervous system. It commonly causes pain, tingling, numbness, and muscle weakness, and can result from injury, toxins, viral illness, diabetes, kidney failure, cancer, or certain drugs.",
